        {"q": "What is Git's object model and what are the four object types?", "a": "Git stores files, folders, commits, and logs", "b": "Git's object model has four types: blob (file content), tree (directory), commit (snapshot metadata), and tag (annotated pointer). All are content-addressed by SHA-1/SHA-256 hash.", "c": "Git uses a relational database internally", "d": "Git stores only commits and branches", "ans": "b", "exp": "Every object is stored in .git/objects/ by its hash. Blobs store file content. Trees reference blobs and other trees. Commits reference trees and parents. Tags reference commits."},
