        {"q": "Why are CNNs particularly effective for image classification tasks?", "a": "Because they process images pixel by pixel sequentially", "b": "Because they exploit local spatial patterns through parameter sharing and local connectivity, requiring far fewer parameters than fully connected networks for the same input size", "c": "Because they use more parameters than any other network", "d": "Because they do not require training", "ans": "b", "exp": "Convolutions use shared filter weights across spatial positions, dramatically reducing parameters and capturing local patterns that are invariant to position."},
