        {"q": "What is the receptive field of a neuron in a CNN?", "a": "The number of filters in a layer", "b": "The region of the input space that influences a particular neuron's activation; deeper layers have larger receptive fields", "c": "The output size of a convolutional layer", "d": "The stride applied to the input", "ans": "b", "exp": "Each neuron in a deeper layer 'sees' a larger area of the input. Stacking convolutional layers increases receptive field size, capturing larger patterns."},
